! LG CX custom rules for AdGuard Home (Filters > Custom filtering rules).
! Adds to HaGeZi's LG webOS list (AdGuard registry filter_72), which missed most of
! what this TV actually contacted on 2026-10-25. Sources: arXiv 2409.06203 (IMC 2024
! ACR study), HaGeZi, Perflyst (+ issue #117), and this TV's own query log / pcaps.

! ---- Never block, whatever a list says ----
! Clock sync at boot: if blocked, the clock resets to 2019 and TLS breaks everywhere
@@||us.lgtvsdp.com^
! Firmware updates (security fixes; note updates have also added ads)
@@||snu.lge.com^
! Possibly the connectivity check; blocking may show "no internet"
@@||lgtvonline.lge.com^
! GFTS file-transfer service: app packages/icons for Content Store installs come from here
! (blocking it broke the Prime Video update on 2026-10-25), but so do the ACR config file, the
! telemetry schedule, LG Shopping data and home-screen promo thumbnails. Since 2026-10-26 the
! four names resolve to the Pi, where nginx (pi/tvgw/nginx-tvgw-gfts.conf) forwards the
! wanted downloads and returns 403 for the rest, logging every URL to /var/log/tvgw/gfts.log.
! (AdGuard's legacy "DNS rewrites" need enabled: true per entry; these rule-based ones don't.)
||ngfts.lge.com^$dnsrewrite=10.10.10.1
||aic-ngfts.lge.com^$dnsrewrite=10.10.10.1
||aic-img-ngfts.lge.com^$dnsrewrite=10.10.10.1
||gfts.lge.com^$dnsrewrite=10.10.10.1

! ---- ACR (LG Ad Solutions / Alphonso): screen fingerprint every ~15 s, even on HDMI ----
||alphonso.tv^

