! ---- ThinQ / IoT / cloud push (user does not use ThinQ; decided 2026-10-25) ----
! lgtviot.com + lgthinq.com are LG's IoT/ThinQ backends; the AWS IoT host is the MQTT push
! channel the TV opened tonight. Unblock all three if you ever want the ThinQ app to control the TV.
||lgtviot.com^
||lgthinq.com^
||a16i6ajbm83mvw-ats.iot.us-west-2.amazonaws.com^

! ---- Voice / speech back-ends (decided 2026-10-26) ----
! The CX has no built-in microphone; the Magic Remote mic is push-to-talk and the TV refuses
! voice recognition while the "Voice Information" agreement is declined (verified: a button press
! produced a consent prompt and zero network activity). These make that a wall, not a checkbox.
! netflixvoice.lgtvcommon.com and lgthinq.com (LG's own speech/AI) are blocked above.
! Not googleapis.com wholesale: YouTube needs www. and youtubei.googleapis.com.
||embeddedassistant.googleapis.com^
||avs-alexa-na.amazon.com^
||avs-alexa-eu.amazon.com^
||avs-alexa-fe.amazon.com^
||api.amazonalexa.com^
||dangbei.com^

